From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PixelOS PIF <pif@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:32:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: accept RKP keyboxes and report attestation state

The keybox importer required both an ECDSA and an RSA block. RKP keyboxes that
reach a STRONG verdict carry only one algorithm, because the framework uses
whichever signing key is present for both leaf algorithms, so the importer
rejected exactly the keyboxes that work.

It also required NumberOfKeyboxes to be a positive integer, while the framework
parser treats it as advisory and only logs a mismatch. The importer must not be
stricter than the code that consumes the file.

Also:

  - Read the registration state back from Settings.Secure in the summary, so a
    keybox that looks configured but is absent from the setting is visible.
    Missing registration was the most common misdiagnosis in the reference
    write-up, and the UI showed the static summary either way.
  - Restart GMS and Play Store after installing or deleting a keybox, since both
    cache attestation material for the life of the process.
  - Accept lowercase "ec" as an algorithm name, which some generators emit.
  - Add an attestation patch level entry (Settings.Secure.tricky_store_patch) so
    the osPatchLevel / vendorPatchLevel / bootPatchLevel written into generated
    attestations can follow a ROM whose OTA lags its security patch.

Base: 9fdea4f2582
